WEBVTT

00:20.840 --> 00:23.472
(TAKE ME AS I AM PLAYING)

00:31.819 --> 00:33.049
♪ I've been lookin' too hard ♪

00:33.084 --> 00:34.383
♪ For a home on the top ♪

00:34.419 --> 00:36.889
♪ On the top
 of the surface searchin' ♪

00:36.924 --> 00:38.519
♪ Lookin' for something deep ♪

00:38.554 --> 00:39.784
 ♪ Thought
 "It's too hard to reach" ♪

00:39.820 --> 00:42.191
♪ Never thought
 I was someone deservin' ♪

00:42.226 --> 00:43.791
♪ But it was all in my head ♪

00:43.826 --> 00:47.530
♪ Heavy weight on my chest
 only ever left me hurtin' ♪

00:47.565 --> 00:50.565
♪ Now I'm callin' a truce
 on the war in my mind ♪

00:50.600 --> 00:53.104
♪ 'Cause I'm finally learnin'
 I'm not ♪

00:53.140 --> 00:55.668
 ♪ Rollin' over, under
 inside out ♪

00:55.703 --> 00:58.473
 ♪ Turnin' myself
 all the way around ♪

00:58.508 --> 01:02.342
 ♪ What you see
 is what you get, so ♪

01:02.377 --> 01:06.211
♪ Baby, you can take me ♪

01:06.247 --> 01:12.224
♪ As I am ♪

01:13.125 --> 01:17.156
♪ Cause' I know I'ma take me ♪

01:17.192 --> 01:22.666
♪ As I am ♪

01:22.701 --> 01:25.537
 ♪ You can take it or leave it
 You can take it or leave it ♪

01:25.572 --> 01:27.701
(VOCALIZING)

01:34.844 --> 01:36.149
Wow.

01:49.530 --> 01:50.596
Hi, Millie!

01:50.632 --> 01:52.994
Hi, Mrs. Winchester!

01:53.030 --> 01:54.061
So nice to meet you.

01:54.097 --> 01:55.331
Please call me Nina.

01:55.367 --> 01:57.266
I've got some tea for us
and a charcuterie board.

01:57.301 --> 01:58.699
Is it too early
for meat and cheese?

01:58.734 --> 02:02.142
You know, that's what they have
for breakfast in Europe.

02:03.241 --> 02:06.278
MILLIE: Wow, um,
you're just, this is...

02:07.075 --> 02:09.076
I... I...

02:09.111 --> 02:12.447
I'm just going to say,
I think you might be
overqualified for this job

02:12.483 --> 02:14.718
with all this experience
and a college degree.

02:14.753 --> 02:15.780
No, I know.

02:15.816 --> 02:18.622
I just realized I really
enjoy being a housemaid.

02:18.657 --> 02:19.518
You do?

02:19.554 --> 02:21.689
For the right families,
of course.

02:22.591 --> 02:25.927
Okay. What brought you back
to New York?

02:25.962 --> 02:27.465
I missed it.

02:27.501 --> 02:30.631
Well, I really love New England,
but I miss being in the city.

02:30.666 --> 02:34.336
But you know this is
a live-in position, right?

02:34.372 --> 02:36.273
I mentioned that in the ad,
didn't I?

02:36.308 --> 02:37.906
Oh, yes. Oh, yeah.
No, of course. Yes. Yes.

02:37.942 --> 02:39.375
Oh, God, okay.

02:39.410 --> 02:41.175
-(EXCLAIMS)
-I miss being near the city,

02:41.211 --> 02:42.945
not actually in the city.

02:42.981 --> 02:44.410
It's a little crazy.

02:44.445 --> 02:47.648
Yes, I fully agree with you.

02:47.684 --> 02:50.682
Okay, so the job is
mostly organizing, cleaning,

02:50.717 --> 02:52.385
light cooking,
if you're up for that.

02:52.421 --> 02:53.921
Oh, absolutely.
I love to cook.

02:53.956 --> 02:55.294
Amazing.

02:55.329 --> 02:56.827
And then you would be
helping me with my daughter.

02:56.863 --> 02:59.198
She's Cecilia, Cece.

02:59.234 --> 03:02.165
She's seven years old
and, well, she's amazing.

03:02.200 --> 03:03.797
Well, I can't wait
to meet her.

03:04.232 --> 03:06.399
Oh. Good. Okay.

03:06.434 --> 03:08.266
Would you like a grand tour

03:08.302 --> 03:10.141
so you can...

03:10.176 --> 03:12.071
see what you're
getting yourself into?

03:12.106 --> 03:13.306
Sure.

03:13.341 --> 03:16.008
NINA: And the kitchen.

03:16.043 --> 03:20.147
My husband, Andrew, designed
this entire house soup to nuts.

03:20.182 --> 03:21.313
He's an architect?

03:21.348 --> 03:22.614
No, he's in tech.

03:22.650 --> 03:25.250
But he pays
incredible attention

03:25.286 --> 03:26.588
to every detail.

03:26.624 --> 03:30.121
Now, these steps are, uh,
kind of nuts, I know.

03:30.157 --> 03:32.892
Andrew says I'm totally gonna
kill myself one day on these.

03:33.426 --> 03:34.926
I'm such a klutz.

03:34.962 --> 03:37.396
I should just draw
my chalk outline on the bottom

03:37.431 --> 03:38.564
and get it over with.

03:38.600 --> 03:39.872
So there's another set
of stairs

03:39.907 --> 03:40.939
on the other side of the house

03:40.974 --> 03:42.708
that are less Guggenheim-y.

03:42.744 --> 03:44.002
If you're into that.

03:48.208 --> 03:49.345
Wow.

03:49.381 --> 03:51.384
NINA: It's basically
Andrew's man cave,

03:51.419 --> 03:55.019
but you are welcome to use it
anytime you want, of course.

03:55.054 --> 03:56.287
You'd be part of the family,

03:56.323 --> 03:58.318
which also means
that you would definitely have

03:58.354 --> 03:59.788
to listen to his TED Talk

03:59.823 --> 04:03.989
about how Barry Lyndon is
a misunderstood masterpiece.

04:06.263 --> 04:08.299
This is the upper living room,

04:08.334 --> 04:10.795
which we barely ever use,
to be honest.

04:10.830 --> 04:13.335
You sure you even need
a housekeeper?

04:13.371 --> 04:16.142
Well, actually,
I'm... expecting.

04:16.177 --> 04:18.207
So I'm not gonna have
quite so much time

04:18.242 --> 04:20.179
to keep everything so perfect.

04:20.215 --> 04:22.942
But don't tell Andrew
because it's very early

04:22.977 --> 04:26.212
and I want to be sure,
you know, before I tell him.

04:26.248 --> 04:27.817
Yeah. Congrats.

04:27.853 --> 04:28.915
Thank you.

04:30.022 --> 04:31.857
This is Cece's room.

04:31.893 --> 04:32.851
Andrew even made a little

04:32.886 --> 04:35.422
miniature version
of our house for her.

04:35.457 --> 04:36.923
-Isn't that sweet?
-Wow.

04:43.204 --> 04:45.334
NINA: So the laundry room is
in the basement,

04:45.370 --> 04:48.104
and that would be
your bathroom

04:48.140 --> 04:50.343
and you would be upstairs.

04:51.839 --> 04:53.913
You're gonna think
it's a little bit small,

04:53.948 --> 04:55.876
but it's got a lot of privacy,

04:55.912 --> 04:58.147
and we figured that that was
the most important thing.

04:58.182 --> 05:00.245
Lots of light, though.

05:00.280 --> 05:01.483
Ta-da!

05:01.518 --> 05:03.388
You can make it your own,
of course.

05:03.424 --> 05:05.785
You can hang posters
and bring in potted plants.

05:05.820 --> 05:07.687
You can blast your music
as loud as you want

05:07.723 --> 05:10.455
because we cannot
hear you downstairs.

05:10.490 --> 05:11.760
What do you think?

05:13.330 --> 05:14.961
-It's perfect.
-Okay, good.

05:16.164 --> 05:17.464
Win!

05:17.499 --> 05:19.138
Well, I'm still interviewing,

05:19.173 --> 05:21.605
but I'm hoping
to make a decision soon.

05:22.677 --> 05:24.076
Here you go.

05:24.112 --> 05:25.140
Oh, no, you don't
have to do that.

05:25.175 --> 05:26.277
Oh, no, I insist.

05:26.312 --> 05:27.443
You spent your energy
and your time

05:27.479 --> 05:29.074
and your gas money
to be here. Please.

05:30.147 --> 05:31.549
I appreciate it.

05:31.585 --> 05:34.983
I have a really good feeling
about this, Millie. I do.

05:35.018 --> 05:36.548
Me too.

05:36.583 --> 05:38.152
Okay. I'll be in touch.

05:38.187 --> 05:39.453
(INAUDIBLE)

05:39.489 --> 05:40.822
MILLIE: She won't be in touch.

05:40.857 --> 05:44.028
That's the last time I'll ever
set foot in that house.

05:44.063 --> 05:45.498
 One background check,

05:45.533 --> 05:48.594
and she'll see that everything
on that resume is a total lie.

05:48.629 --> 05:50.434
 I don't even wear glasses.

05:50.469 --> 05:52.397
 I'm just...
 I'm trying to look legit.

05:52.432 --> 05:53.703
 So stupid.

06:00.442 --> 06:02.008
(HAND DRYER BLOWING)

06:08.252 --> 06:09.950
-Here you go.
-Thanks.

06:12.655 --> 06:14.254
Um, can I get
a job application?

06:14.289 --> 06:15.961
Yeah, sure.

06:15.996 --> 06:17.694
-There you go.
-Thanks.

06:26.303 --> 06:27.539
(HAND DRYER BLOWING)

06:28.374 --> 06:30.003
MILLIE: I knew
 she wouldn't call.

06:30.038 --> 06:31.937
 Why did I even think I had
 a shot at that job?

06:31.972 --> 06:34.975
 Oh, well, at least I got
 $20 out of it.

06:36.581 --> 06:38.748
(SIGHS) I don't know
 what I'm gonna do.

06:48.929 --> 06:49.957
Roll it down.

06:52.394 --> 06:53.899
Can't sleep here.

06:53.934 --> 06:55.630
I'm so sorry. I...

06:55.665 --> 06:57.233
I was driving
from my mom's house

06:57.268 --> 06:58.569
and I got really sleepy,

06:58.605 --> 07:00.334
and I just I pulled over
to take a nap. I'm sorry.

07:00.369 --> 07:02.804
(PHONE VIBRATING)

07:02.840 --> 07:04.538
This is her actually.
Do you mind if I take it?

07:04.573 --> 07:05.912
She's probably freaking out.

07:05.947 --> 07:07.407
Don't text and drive.

07:07.443 --> 07:08.877
I won't. I promise.

07:12.045 --> 07:14.547
-Hello?
 -Hi, may I speak to Millie?

07:14.582 --> 07:17.220
Uh, this is her. She.

07:17.256 --> 07:18.983
 This is Nina Winchester.

07:19.019 --> 07:20.985
 I'm calling
 to offer you the job.

07:21.020 --> 07:23.627
 I mean, if you're
 still available.

07:23.663 --> 07:25.594
 Uh, you've probably got
 a million job offers.

07:25.629 --> 07:27.662
No. I mean, yes, yes.
I would love to.

07:27.697 --> 07:29.864
Uh, when would
you like me to start?

07:29.900 --> 07:33.600
 Oh, my goodness. (SIGHS)
 As soon as possible?

07:33.636 --> 07:35.071
Well, what about
this afternoon?

07:35.107 --> 07:36.307
 You know what?

07:36.343 --> 07:37.903
 -That would be great.
-Great.

07:37.938 --> 07:39.743
 Anyway, gotta run.
 Bye, Millie.

07:40.278 --> 07:41.646
MILLIE: (SOFTLY) Yes!

07:50.519 --> 07:53.119
-(CLICK)
-(LINE RINGING)

07:55.697 --> 07:56.760
Hey!

07:58.266 --> 07:59.363
-Hey, I'm Millie.
-(LINE RINGING)

07:59.399 --> 08:01.896
Do you work
for the Winchesters?

08:01.932 --> 08:04.430
I'm trying to get in,
but I don't know the code.

08:04.465 --> 08:05.497
(LINE BEEPS)

08:05.533 --> 08:06.770
(GATES CLANK)

08:30.765 --> 08:31.795
Nina?

08:33.660 --> 08:35.095
Nina, it's Millie.

08:41.039 --> 08:42.069
Nina?

08:51.110 --> 08:53.212
NINA: Millie?
Millie, Millie, Millie!

08:54.055 --> 08:55.421
(EXCLAIMS) Welcome. Hi.

08:55.456 --> 08:57.349
Sorry. I, um, meant
to leave the gate open.

08:57.384 --> 09:00.289
Do you need me to help you bring
in your stuff from your car?

09:00.325 --> 09:01.621
Oh, no, this is it.

09:01.656 --> 09:03.793
-Great. Wow.
-Yeah.

09:03.829 --> 09:05.456
Yeah, no, I put the rest of it
in a storage unit.

09:05.492 --> 09:07.894
Okay, well, that's great. I'm
gonna put these up in your room.

09:07.929 --> 09:10.796
Listen, I need
to write a PTA speech

09:10.831 --> 09:12.899
that has to be a barn burner,

09:12.934 --> 09:14.366
so I'm gonna be
stuck in my office.

09:14.401 --> 09:16.609
But the cleaning supplies are
in this closet over there,

09:17.044 --> 09:19.278
and... um, oh.

09:19.314 --> 09:21.273
You're not wearing
your glasses.

09:21.308 --> 09:24.342
Oh, I don't... I don't wear 'em
all the time. Contacts.

09:26.018 --> 09:27.111
Oh.

09:27.146 --> 09:28.984
Yeah, you look better
without them.

09:29.924 --> 09:31.085
Yeah. Okay.

09:31.586 --> 09:33.687
I'll be upstairs.

09:33.722 --> 09:35.186
This is gonna be fun, Millie!

09:35.221 --> 09:37.223
(TUMBLING DICE BY
LINDA RONSTADT PLAYING)

09:41.263 --> 09:45.637
♪ People try to rape me
 Always think I'm crazy ♪

09:45.673 --> 09:49.301
♪ Make me burn
 the candle right down ♪

09:50.539 --> 09:52.444
♪ Baby ♪

09:52.479 --> 09:54.542
(SONG CONTINUES PLAYING
ON HEADPHONES)

09:54.578 --> 09:56.308
No shoes on the furniture.

10:00.020 --> 10:02.615
Um, hey. Hi.

10:02.651 --> 10:05.383
You must be... Cece.

10:06.059 --> 10:07.286
I'm Millie.

10:08.093 --> 10:09.123
Hello.

10:09.857 --> 10:12.194
Oh, hey. Hi! You met Millie.

10:12.230 --> 10:13.057
Hi, baby.

10:13.093 --> 10:15.167
Millie's gonna be
living with us,

10:15.203 --> 10:16.027
and she's gonna be helping

10:16.063 --> 10:17.366
with the cooking
and the cleaning.

10:17.401 --> 10:18.603
And you know what?

10:18.638 --> 10:20.131
She might even play
 Candy Land with you

10:20.166 --> 10:22.405
if you ask her
with a pretty please.

10:22.441 --> 10:23.904
She's gonna live with us?

10:23.939 --> 10:26.339
(LAUGHING) Yes.
Andrew, I told you that.

10:26.375 --> 10:30.549
I said she was gonna be living
in the guest room in the attic.

10:30.585 --> 10:33.048
Doesn't this place look
incredible. Look at it.

10:35.687 --> 10:38.287
-Thank you.
-Well, Millie, welcome.

10:38.323 --> 10:39.687
Uh, thank you.

10:39.723 --> 10:41.022
Are you hungry?
I'm sure we can

10:41.058 --> 10:42.626
turn this dinner for three
into a dinner for four.

10:42.661 --> 10:44.725
No, I'm probably
just gonna go upstairs

10:44.760 --> 10:47.058
and, uh, get all settled in.

10:47.093 --> 10:48.292
-You sure?
-If you don't mind,

10:48.327 --> 10:50.866
I'll just come down afterwards
and tidy up.

10:50.901 --> 10:53.031
Yeah, get settled.
Yeah, take your time.

10:53.067 --> 10:54.540
We're so happy
that you're here.

10:54.575 --> 10:56.170
You just let us know
if you change your mind.

10:57.109 --> 10:58.172
Thanks.

11:03.376 --> 11:05.443
You ordered from the wrong
Italian place again.

11:41.651 --> 11:42.887
NINA: Knock, knock.

11:44.255 --> 11:45.082
Hi.

11:45.117 --> 11:47.286
That window doesn't open, sadly.

11:47.321 --> 11:49.188
But there's a lot
of ventilation in this room,

11:49.223 --> 11:51.230
so you should never
get stuffy in here.

11:51.265 --> 11:52.594
I got you some dinner.

11:52.630 --> 11:55.298
Andrew always over-orders.

11:55.334 --> 11:56.260
I put some water

11:56.296 --> 11:57.635
in the mini fridge,
did you see that?

11:57.671 --> 11:59.266
Yeah, I really don't
want to be a pain,

11:59.301 --> 12:02.036
but if it is possible to try
and get the window open,

12:02.071 --> 12:04.202
it'd be nice to get
some fresh air in here.

12:04.237 --> 12:06.744
Yeah, I agree.
That's a great idea.

12:06.779 --> 12:08.506
I will talk to the handyman
about that.

12:08.541 --> 12:11.209
Okay, cool. Is that the guy
that's down in the yard?

12:11.244 --> 12:13.415
No, that's Enzo.
He's the groundskeeper.

12:13.451 --> 12:14.787
Never mind him.

12:14.822 --> 12:16.817
And then if I could just
get a key for the deadbolt.

12:16.852 --> 12:19.787
Oh, my God, yes. The deadbolt.

12:19.822 --> 12:22.620
(CHUCKLES) That's so creepy.

12:22.655 --> 12:26.461
This used to be Andrew's storage
closet for his files. Okay?

12:26.497 --> 12:27.932
But, oh, my God,

12:28.434 --> 12:30.330
closed window, deadbolt.

12:31.966 --> 12:33.636
What kind of monsters are we?

12:33.672 --> 12:35.505
-Uh...
-I will sort that out.

12:35.541 --> 12:37.205
Oh, before I forget. Um...

12:38.808 --> 12:40.440
This is for you. A present.

12:40.475 --> 12:43.547
Also, just, I saw that your
phone was just really ancient,

12:43.582 --> 12:45.816
and I wanted you to have that

12:45.851 --> 12:48.686
because I uploaded
the credit card onto it

12:48.722 --> 12:49.748
so you can use it
at the grocery store

12:49.783 --> 12:51.053
and for gas.

12:51.088 --> 12:53.486
Oh, um, I'll take good care
of it. Thank you.

12:53.521 --> 12:58.897
Honestly, I'm like, so happy
that... you're here with us.

12:59.561 --> 13:00.926
Thanks.

13:00.961 --> 13:02.494
Can I give you a hug?

13:04.471 --> 13:06.336
(SIGHS) Thank you, Millie.

13:06.372 --> 13:08.332
Thank you. Okay.

13:08.368 --> 13:10.205
Let me know
if you need anything else.

13:27.820 --> 13:29.224
(YAWNS)

13:35.531 --> 13:36.561
Shit.

13:44.804 --> 13:46.043
(CLICKS)

13:46.544 --> 13:49.247
(LOCK RATTLES)

13:49.282 --> 13:50.109
No, no, no.

13:50.145 --> 13:52.547
-(STRAINING)
-(DOORKNOB RATTLING)

13:52.582 --> 13:53.952
No, no, no.

13:54.453 --> 13:55.954
(DOOR CREAKS)

13:58.852 --> 14:00.090
(SHRIEKING)

14:07.563 --> 14:09.064
Nina?

14:09.099 --> 14:11.032
-(SHOUTING) Where are they?
-Where are what?

14:11.067 --> 14:13.232
My PTA notes
for the meeting tonight!

14:13.267 --> 14:14.703
They were right here
on the counter,

14:14.739 --> 14:15.839
and now they're not here.

14:15.874 --> 14:17.274
-Where are they?
-I didn't see any notes.

14:17.310 --> 14:18.540
Bullshit!

14:18.576 --> 14:19.604
Where are they?

14:20.845 --> 14:22.612
-Nina, no, no.
-ANDREW: Hey.

14:22.647 --> 14:23.948
Hey! What's going on?

14:23.984 --> 14:27.645
Millie threw away my notes
for the meeting tonight.

14:29.182 --> 14:31.088
(SHOUTING) Where are they?

14:32.892 --> 14:34.823
Nina, why don't we go
check your office?

14:34.859 --> 14:36.725
I have to get up
and do a speech

14:36.760 --> 14:37.957
in front of everybody

14:37.992 --> 14:39.291
and now I have nothing!

14:39.326 --> 14:41.764
-(OBJECTS CLATTERING)
-(SHRIEKING)

14:41.800 --> 14:43.568
-ANDREW: Nina!
-(YELLING) What?

14:43.604 --> 14:45.837
-(DRAWER SLIDING SHUT)
-(THUDS)

14:45.872 --> 14:48.072
-Do you have a copy...
-(VESSELS CLINKING)

14:48.640 --> 14:49.870
...on your computer?

14:49.905 --> 14:52.010
I wrote them by hand!

14:52.543 --> 14:54.175
Oh, fuck!

14:54.211 --> 14:56.513
I always think better
when I write by hand.

14:56.549 --> 14:58.082
Where's my nail at?

14:58.683 --> 15:00.249
(SHRIEKS AND WHIMPERS)

15:00.814 --> 15:05.153
(CRYING)

15:05.188 --> 15:06.788
ANDREW: All right.
Come here, come here.

15:06.824 --> 15:08.961
-(CRYING)
-It's okay.

15:10.428 --> 15:13.798
(CRYING)

15:13.834 --> 15:16.067
ANDREW: Let's take
a deep breath, okay?

15:16.102 --> 15:18.331
-(NINA CONTINUES CRYING)
-Breathe, breathe, breathe.

15:18.366 --> 15:20.802
-Breathe, breathe, breathe.
-(SNIFFLES)

15:20.837 --> 15:23.041
(EXHALES AND SNIFFLES)

15:23.642 --> 15:24.944
I'm gonna pick you up.

15:28.012 --> 15:29.314
-(NINA CRIES)
-(ANDREW GRUNTS SOFTLY)

15:29.350 --> 15:31.577
(NINA SOBBING)

15:35.649 --> 15:38.652
Here's the plan. I am going
to take Cece to school,

15:38.688 --> 15:40.385
and you...

15:40.420 --> 15:42.828
you are going to take
a hot shower.

15:42.863 --> 15:44.358
You're gonna have
a nice long breakfast,

15:44.394 --> 15:46.295
and then you have all day
to work on your speech,

15:46.331 --> 15:49.595
and you can still make it
to the salon for a touch up.

15:49.630 --> 15:51.568
You'll have just enough time
to get your roots done.

15:51.604 --> 15:52.802
I love you so much.

15:52.837 --> 15:54.204
-I love you.
-I love you.

15:57.272 --> 15:59.539
You need to be
more careful next time.

16:01.648 --> 16:03.312
You've ruined my entire day.

16:04.978 --> 16:06.216
I'm sorry.

16:11.425 --> 16:12.651
(ANDREW SIGHS)

16:15.055 --> 16:16.292
I am so sorry.

16:17.598 --> 16:18.689
Don-- Don't worry about it.

16:18.725 --> 16:20.430
I don't know what's been
going on with her lately.

16:20.465 --> 16:22.066
She's...

16:22.101 --> 16:24.735
she's been on a real
emotional roller coaster.

16:24.770 --> 16:26.500
Oh, it's probably the hor--

16:27.905 --> 16:30.105
um, Mercury in retrograde.

16:30.140 --> 16:31.969
Didn't peg you
for the star-chart type.

16:32.004 --> 16:33.408
Guilty.

16:36.650 --> 16:38.215
Let me help you clean up.

16:38.250 --> 16:39.783
-It's a fuckin' mess in here.
-No, no, no. I got it.

16:39.818 --> 16:41.919
I got it. You go get ready.

16:41.954 --> 16:43.451
I don't want you
to be late for Cece.

16:44.556 --> 16:45.651
Thank you.

16:48.589 --> 16:51.228
-(TAPS COUNTERTOP)
-Tomorrow will be better.

16:53.227 --> 16:55.199
It'll be better, I promise.

16:55.764 --> 16:56.794
Okay.

17:02.302 --> 17:03.872
-Yeah.
-(TAPS COUNTERTOP)

17:03.908 --> 17:06.276
Cece! Let's hit the road!

17:07.746 --> 17:09.543
(OMINOUS MUSIC PLAYS)

17:26.528 --> 17:28.133
(IN NON-NATIVE ACCENT)
What are you doing here?

17:28.732 --> 17:30.102
I work here.

17:31.033 --> 17:32.698
What are you doing here?

17:33.604 --> 17:35.140
You...

17:43.144 --> 17:47.119
(MUTTERS IN ITALIAN)

18:03.263 --> 18:04.730
-(YAWNS)
-(BUCKET THUDS)

18:09.907 --> 18:12.705
(EERIE MUSIC PLAYING)

18:25.353 --> 18:27.087
I don't really
fit in very well

18:27.123 --> 18:29.161
with those other PTA moms.

18:30.394 --> 18:33.056
I guess I didn't realize
how stressed I've been.

18:33.092 --> 18:36.696
It's probably just all the new
hormones making you go crazy.

18:39.335 --> 18:41.032
I wouldn't say anything
to Andrew.

18:41.067 --> 18:42.405
Get out.

18:42.939 --> 18:44.074
I have to shower.

18:44.109 --> 18:45.939
And you're gonna
handle dinner later.

18:45.975 --> 18:47.212
MILLIE: Yeah.

18:47.979 --> 18:49.110
ANDREW: It smells amazing.

18:49.145 --> 18:50.944
MILLIE: It's chicken piccata.

18:50.979 --> 18:52.212
ANDREW: Mmm.

18:52.247 --> 18:54.448
Oh, I picked this up for Cece.

18:54.484 --> 18:57.417
Oh, these are fantastic.
She's gonna love these.

18:57.452 --> 18:58.650
Someone did not
get her snack today,

18:58.685 --> 19:01.055
and she's a very hungry
little ballerina.

19:01.090 --> 19:02.558
(MILLIE CHUCKLES SOFTLY)

19:02.593 --> 19:05.023
Why don't you get her started,
and I'll be right back down?

19:05.058 --> 19:06.462
Okay.

19:08.963 --> 19:10.268
(SIGHS)

19:12.198 --> 19:13.634
Hey, Cece,

19:14.003 --> 19:15.339
how was class?

19:16.874 --> 19:18.043
(BREATHES DEEPLY)

19:18.078 --> 19:21.472
Would you, uh, like juice
or... or water?

19:21.508 --> 19:24.249
Juice.
But this glass is dirty.

19:25.185 --> 19:26.949
Really? I just took it out
of the dishwasher.

19:26.984 --> 19:28.251
Juice is a privilege.

19:28.287 --> 19:30.717
Not something you drink
out of a dirty glass.

19:32.153 --> 19:33.423
Of course not.

19:34.725 --> 19:35.755
(SIGHS)

19:46.872 --> 19:48.603
This looks amazing.

19:48.638 --> 19:51.540
Doesn't it, Cece? Way better
than dinosaur nuggets.

19:53.239 --> 19:54.773
Hey, Millie,

19:54.808 --> 19:57.678
why don't you grab
a place setting and join us?

19:58.683 --> 19:59.718
Uh...

19:59.753 --> 20:01.179
No, I... I already ate.

20:01.215 --> 20:02.485
Oh, we insist.

20:03.316 --> 20:04.784
Don't we, Cece?

20:07.054 --> 20:08.293
Um...

20:09.323 --> 20:10.955
I hope you guys like it.

20:30.948 --> 20:32.548
(KNOCKING AT DOOR)

20:33.718 --> 20:34.847
Come in.

20:37.216 --> 20:39.220
Hey.

20:39.256 --> 20:41.425
-Hey.
-Sorry to bother you.

20:42.928 --> 20:44.255
Got something for you.

20:44.291 --> 20:45.660
Cece insisted.

20:46.525 --> 20:48.564
-She's so sweet.
-Yeah.

20:50.765 --> 20:53.701
(WHY IS SHE STILL HERE?
BY RENEE RAPP PLAYING)

20:57.603 --> 20:59.977
♪ You can tell me ♪

21:00.012 --> 21:01.807
♪ You don't love her ♪

21:01.843 --> 21:05.115
♪ But you should
 probably tell her too ♪

21:05.150 --> 21:06.243
♪ 'Cause I can't keep... ♪

21:06.278 --> 21:07.550
(GASPS)

21:08.050 --> 21:09.282
No, no, no.

21:09.317 --> 21:11.653
Absolutely fucking not!

21:12.692 --> 21:13.721
Oh, my God.

21:22.430 --> 21:24.633
I want you to feel safe here.

21:26.705 --> 21:27.735
I do.

21:30.504 --> 21:32.410
For your door, as requested.

21:32.942 --> 21:34.478
Thanks.

21:38.085 --> 21:40.418
So how was last night?
With Andrew?

21:41.852 --> 21:43.316
Good.

21:43.351 --> 21:44.983
I made chicken piccata.

21:46.189 --> 21:47.986
He's a dream, isn't he?

21:49.493 --> 21:51.290
He pretends to like everything
I make him,

21:51.326 --> 21:52.562
even if he hates it.

21:58.099 --> 21:59.371
Mmm.

22:02.074 --> 22:04.040
That's a lot of bacon, Millie.

22:04.076 --> 22:05.773
Are you trying to kill us?

22:11.379 --> 22:12.747
Where are you going?

22:15.018 --> 22:16.215
I have...

22:16.251 --> 22:17.550
Saturday off.

22:17.586 --> 22:18.682
Isn't that
what we talked about?

22:18.718 --> 22:21.723
No, I...
I can't spare you today.

22:22.591 --> 22:24.625
I missed
my hair salon appointment

22:24.660 --> 22:28.094
because you threw away
my notes. (CHUCKLES)

22:28.130 --> 22:29.727
Remember?

22:29.763 --> 22:32.835
I have a meeting
that I can't miss.

22:32.870 --> 22:34.135
(SCOFFS)

22:34.171 --> 22:35.539
You have a meeting?

22:36.107 --> 22:37.541
What's the meeting for?

22:40.379 --> 22:42.012
If I could just have
a couple hours off,

22:42.047 --> 22:43.079
and then I'll come back.

22:43.114 --> 22:45.415
Millie, absolutely not.

22:45.450 --> 22:47.251
-ANDREW: Baby?
-I can't have you... What?

22:47.286 --> 22:49.520
Sweetheart, it's okay.
She can go.

22:51.018 --> 22:53.118
-But, Andy, it's your day off.
-I know, exactly.

22:53.154 --> 22:56.591
And that's why we're gonna go
to the park... fly this kite.

22:56.627 --> 22:57.756
And we've been waiting
all week to fly, right?

22:57.792 --> 22:58.722
We're doing donuts,
we're doing kites,

22:58.757 --> 23:00.465
and then we're doing ballet.

23:02.034 --> 23:03.061
Go. Take your time.

23:07.040 --> 23:09.166
-Bye, Mama.
-Bye, baby.

23:11.405 --> 23:14.679
(BREATHES DEEPLY)

23:14.715 --> 23:15.843
Have fun.

23:20.346 --> 23:21.618
Thanks.

23:23.955 --> 23:25.050
(DOOR OPENS)

23:27.027 --> 23:28.453
PAM: Hey, how are you doin'?

23:28.488 --> 23:30.226
MILLIE: I'm good.

23:30.261 --> 23:31.657
Still writing in your journal?

23:31.693 --> 23:34.633
Uh, yeah.
Do you wanna read it?

23:34.668 --> 23:35.563
God, no.

23:35.598 --> 23:38.335
I have enough shit
to read as it is.

23:38.370 --> 23:40.638
So you left the job
at Charlie's?

23:40.673 --> 23:44.475
Well, this housekeeping job
just sort of fell into my lap.

23:44.511 --> 23:47.043
And it's live-in,
so I'm saving a fortune on rent.

23:47.078 --> 23:49.113
Okay, that's good.

23:49.148 --> 23:52.015
I have my new address here,

23:52.050 --> 23:53.579
and phone number.

23:53.614 --> 23:56.053
The family is really amazing.

23:56.088 --> 23:57.555
I feel... I feel lucky.

23:57.590 --> 23:59.783
Must make meeting new people
a little tough, though,

23:59.818 --> 24:01.391
having to live with a family.

24:01.426 --> 24:02.791
I mean, you would
think that, right?

24:02.826 --> 24:06.791
But I have already met
a ton of really cool nannies.

24:06.827 --> 24:08.632
Any mannies in there?
(CHUCKLES)

24:09.534 --> 24:12.400
Are you asking me
about my love life, Pam?

24:12.435 --> 24:13.767
If I know how Tinder works,

24:13.802 --> 24:16.638
or if I'm horn dogging
all over Great Neck

24:16.674 --> 24:18.004
because I haven't gotten laid
in ten years?

24:18.039 --> 24:20.908
No. I'm just saying
human connections are important.

24:22.277 --> 24:23.543
Definitely.

24:23.579 --> 24:25.682
But hold onto this job,
Millie.

24:26.383 --> 24:27.783
And the living situation.

24:29.720 --> 24:31.917
You'll need both,
or you'll be back at Bedford

24:31.953 --> 24:35.357
serving the five years
left on your sentence.

24:35.392 --> 24:37.591
And I don't like that for you.

24:37.627 --> 24:39.795
I don't like that
for me, either.

24:42.628 --> 24:45.229
(PHONE VIBRATING)

24:48.641 --> 24:50.441
-Hi, Nina, I'm just--
 -I need you to pick up Cece

24:50.477 --> 24:53.373
 from ballet class, 1:45,
 and don't be late.

24:53.408 --> 24:54.607
(LINE DISCONNECTS)

24:54.642 --> 24:57.648
Um, okay, where is it? Nina?

24:59.280 --> 25:00.618
What?

25:01.988 --> 25:03.214
Ballet school?

25:03.649 --> 25:04.886
Ballet class.

25:06.893 --> 25:08.320
Little kids.

25:08.355 --> 25:10.094
Fuck.

25:10.129 --> 25:11.493
INSTRUCTOR: Tendu right.

25:11.529 --> 25:14.998
And curtsy
and open to the left.

25:15.034 --> 25:16.332
Foot behind you.

25:16.367 --> 25:18.863
Excellent, and close to first.

25:18.899 --> 25:20.766
Fabulous class today.
Thank you.

25:20.802 --> 25:22.933
Let's go get
our bags and shoes.

25:22.969 --> 25:25.610
-Great job.
-(DOORBELL CHIMING)

25:26.677 --> 25:29.673
-Hi. Who are you looking for?
-Uh, Cece.

25:29.709 --> 25:31.544
Cecilia Winchester.

25:31.579 --> 25:32.947
Are you Nina's new girl?

25:33.714 --> 25:36.280
-Yes. Hi, I'm Millie.
-Hi.

25:37.616 --> 25:38.883
MILLIE: Hi!

25:38.919 --> 25:41.655
Cece! Hey,
I'm here to pick you up.

25:41.691 --> 25:43.792
I'm spending the night
at Emma's.

25:43.828 --> 25:46.557
We arranged it weeks ago.
She has all her things.

25:46.593 --> 25:47.895
Oh, no, no, no.

25:47.931 --> 25:49.531
Nina just called me
and asked me to pick her up,

25:49.567 --> 25:50.968
so she probably
changed her mind.

25:51.003 --> 25:52.566
PATRICE: Oh.

25:52.601 --> 25:54.265
(EXHALES) Okay, let me check.

25:58.570 --> 25:59.842
Nina!

26:00.310 --> 26:02.544
Hi, it's Patrice.

26:02.580 --> 26:04.445
Your girl is here.
She's insisting

26:04.481 --> 26:06.981
she needs to pick up Cece.

26:09.253 --> 26:10.853
(PATRICE CHUCKLES)

26:12.188 --> 26:13.284
I know.

26:13.959 --> 26:14.918
I know.

26:14.953 --> 26:16.922
No, it's no problem at all.

26:16.957 --> 26:19.598
It's impossible to find
reliable help.

26:20.299 --> 26:22.428
Oh, would you like to confirm?

26:22.464 --> 26:23.932
(MILLIE INHALES)

26:24.905 --> 26:26.033
Have fun.

26:28.206 --> 26:29.536
We figured it out.

26:29.571 --> 26:32.171
Okay, take care. Bye.

26:32.939 --> 26:34.908
Wow,
they really are beautiful.

26:34.943 --> 26:37.081
NINA: So happy
we'll be able to use them,

26:37.116 --> 26:38.175
Mother Winchester.

26:38.210 --> 26:41.015
Well, the pattern is vintage,
of course.

26:41.648 --> 26:42.918
NINA: Millie.

26:45.152 --> 26:47.622
I told you Cece was having
a sleepover tonight.

26:47.658 --> 26:49.888
There was no need
to make a scene.

26:49.924 --> 26:51.421
-(MILLIE INHALES)
-(MOTHER SIGHS)

26:51.456 --> 26:55.566
This is how you allow the help
to dress in your home?

26:55.601 --> 26:57.596
Uh, this is Andrew's mother,
Mrs. Winchester.

26:57.631 --> 26:58.833
She's downsizing,

26:58.868 --> 27:00.997
so she has brought us
her mother's china.

27:01.033 --> 27:02.773
-Yes.
-NINA: Isn't it lovely?

27:04.109 --> 27:05.677
Isn't it?

27:06.409 --> 27:08.377
-Yes.
-I know.

27:08.413 --> 27:11.012
Andrew loves these dishes.

27:11.579 --> 27:13.646
I want you...

27:13.682 --> 27:15.179
to put them somewhere safe

27:15.214 --> 27:17.915
'cause Nina's likely
to trip over herself

27:17.950 --> 27:19.687
and smash them all to pieces.

27:19.723 --> 27:20.887
-(MOTHER CHUCKLES)
-(DOOR OPENS)

27:20.922 --> 27:22.854
-Guilty as charged.
-(DOOR CLOSES)

27:22.889 --> 27:24.561
-MOTHER: Andrew!
-ANDREW: Oh.

27:24.596 --> 27:27.125
-Mother.
-Oh, Andrew, where's your tie?

27:27.160 --> 27:29.897
ANDREW: I know,
I'm too casual. I'm sorry.

27:29.932 --> 27:31.829
-Your hair is fabulous.
-Thank you, darling.

27:31.865 --> 27:34.000
Not a root in sight. Is...

27:34.035 --> 27:35.704
-Is that what I think it is?
-Yes, it is.

27:35.739 --> 27:37.703
Can't wait to eat off
of those plates.

27:37.739 --> 27:39.409
MOTHER: Family heirlooms.

27:39.444 --> 27:41.372
-So happy it's back.
-Me too.

27:45.182 --> 27:46.443
(SIGHS)

27:47.850 --> 27:50.084
This fucking window.
(GROANS SOFTLY)

27:54.721 --> 27:56.656
(GROANS SOFTLY)

27:56.691 --> 27:58.224
(WOOD SQUEAKING SOFTLY)

28:19.578 --> 28:21.115
(WOMAN SPEAKING ON TV)
 Dishes are still in the sink.

28:21.150 --> 28:23.147
MAN 1: Yeah, I know.
 I'm kinda lettin' em soak.

28:23.182 --> 28:24.587
WOMAN: Uh,
 they've been soaking

28:24.622 --> 28:26.283
 -for three days.
-(LAUGH TRACK)

28:26.318 --> 28:27.724
MAN: Well, now,
 you know, it's kinda...

28:27.759 --> 28:29.754
 Glug, glug, glug,
 glug, glug. Ding.

28:29.790 --> 28:31.496
 Glug, glug, glug.

28:31.531 --> 28:33.028
 ...home
 with everybody going out.

28:33.861 --> 28:34.925
 I'm going to ask you one...

28:34.960 --> 28:36.768
(SPEAKING INDISTINCTLY)

28:38.232 --> 28:40.000
MAN: I'm not gonna ask you
 what you sell.

28:40.036 --> 28:42.240
 I'm gonna go on here
 to Patsy, all right?

28:42.275 --> 28:43.775
ANDREW: Ah, Family Feud.

28:44.210 --> 28:45.872
I'm so sorry.

28:45.908 --> 28:47.677
Um... I...
I couldn't get some...

28:47.712 --> 28:48.943
-I'll leave you alone.
-No, no. Please.

28:48.979 --> 28:50.146
-Get out of your way.
-Sit, please. No, sit.

28:50.181 --> 28:51.442
Come on.

28:52.844 --> 28:54.516
Please stay.

28:54.551 --> 28:56.788
Oh, I love this show.

28:57.254 --> 28:58.953
Me too.

28:58.988 --> 29:01.592
I've only ever seen
the Steve Harvey one.

29:01.627 --> 29:03.690
-Really? Oh, this is classic.
-Yeah.

29:03.725 --> 29:05.195
This is Richard Dawson.

29:05.231 --> 29:06.765
Fashion icon.

29:07.333 --> 29:09.666
-He's an OG.
-Yeah?

29:09.701 --> 29:11.762
He has
some spectacular sideburns.

29:11.798 --> 29:13.463
He sure does.

29:13.498 --> 29:16.638
Man, my family would have
killed on this show.

29:16.673 --> 29:18.441
They are absolute vultures.

29:18.476 --> 29:19.510
Especially my mother.

29:19.546 --> 29:21.841
What about you?
You... your, um...

29:21.876 --> 29:23.342
parents, are they game people?

29:24.750 --> 29:27.347
Oh, we don't really
keep in touch anymore.

29:27.383 --> 29:28.415
Oh.

29:28.451 --> 29:29.480
I'm sorry.

29:30.422 --> 29:31.981
That's gotta be hard.

29:32.017 --> 29:34.385
Uh, not really, no.

29:34.421 --> 29:36.553
I mean, even if we were,
they probably wouldn't...

29:37.263 --> 29:38.860
be into this.

29:38.896 --> 29:41.332
They're kinda like
the opposite of fun.

29:41.368 --> 29:42.460
Well, I'll tell you what.

29:43.765 --> 29:45.232
You can be on our team.

29:46.603 --> 29:47.971
It'd be me and you...

29:49.001 --> 29:50.707
and Nina and my mom.

29:50.742 --> 29:52.536
Nina's parents don't
make the cut?

29:53.204 --> 29:55.110
They died when she was a kid.

29:55.876 --> 29:57.882
-That's awful.
-Yeah.

29:58.748 --> 30:00.351
It's a crazy story, actually.

30:00.387 --> 30:01.919
They died in a house fire.

30:02.853 --> 30:05.755
No one knows
how it was started.

30:05.791 --> 30:07.420
Nina made it out,
her parents didn't.

30:07.455 --> 30:10.158
For a long time, the police
actually thought that she...

30:14.696 --> 30:16.633
Can you imagine...

30:16.669 --> 30:19.033
living with that
your entire life?

30:19.068 --> 30:21.400
-That'd be terrible.
-What would be terrible?

30:22.936 --> 30:24.172
ANDREW: There she is.

30:24.605 --> 30:25.740
Hey.

30:25.775 --> 30:27.945
RICHARD: Name a cartoon bird.

30:28.545 --> 30:29.743
(BUZZER BEEPING)

30:29.778 --> 30:31.079
What are you doing up?

30:31.115 --> 30:33.043
What do you mean?
I can say the same about you.

30:33.079 --> 30:34.877
I'm watching Family Feud.

30:34.913 --> 30:36.083
NINA: Mmm.

30:36.118 --> 30:37.887
-At 2:00 a.m.?
-You wanna get in on this?

30:37.922 --> 30:40.457
Some Dawson? Wanna get
some Dawson on you?

30:40.492 --> 30:42.223
No, I'm good. It's...

30:42.956 --> 30:44.192
Baby, it's 2:00 a.m.

30:44.625 --> 30:45.897
Okay.

30:46.399 --> 30:47.860
I'mma go to bed. (SIGHS)

30:47.895 --> 30:49.428
Let me know how it ends.

30:51.270 --> 30:52.332
All right.

30:54.702 --> 30:55.940
Goodnight.

30:56.674 --> 30:58.503
-I'll be right up.
-Okay.

30:59.679 --> 31:02.006
 Uh, cartoon bird,
 little Katie.

31:02.042 --> 31:03.107
 Three answers remaining.

31:03.142 --> 31:04.748
-KATIE: Daffy Duck.
-Um.

31:04.784 --> 31:06.014
RICHARD: Let's see
 if you made it.

31:06.049 --> 31:09.387
It's late. I should
probably get some sleep.

31:09.422 --> 31:10.618
(PEOPLE CHEERING ON TV)

31:10.653 --> 31:11.685
(REMOTE CLICKING)

31:11.721 --> 31:13.122
This isn't working.

31:13.856 --> 31:16.191
-What?
-This isn't working.

31:17.225 --> 31:19.829
So I'm gonna need you
to pack your stuff

31:19.864 --> 31:21.091
and leave
first thing in the morning

31:21.126 --> 31:22.626
before Cece wakes up.

31:23.470 --> 31:24.498
So she doesn't get upset.

31:24.534 --> 31:26.333
No, Nina.

31:27.537 --> 31:28.598
I... I...

31:28.633 --> 31:30.368
I didn't think anyone was
gonna be down here.

31:30.403 --> 31:32.039
You told me I could use
the screening room.

31:32.074 --> 31:33.805
I'm gonna need
the phone back as well.

31:33.841 --> 31:35.646
Please, Nina.

31:35.682 --> 31:37.648
-(SCOFFING)
-I will do anything

31:37.684 --> 31:39.384
to make it up to you.
I promise.

31:39.419 --> 31:40.479
Can you just give me...

31:41.354 --> 31:42.382
one more chance?

31:44.323 --> 31:45.385
(NINA SIGHS)

31:45.884 --> 31:47.123
Um...

31:47.622 --> 31:48.685
Fine.

31:50.263 --> 31:51.292
One week.

31:51.758 --> 31:53.160
Okay?

31:53.195 --> 31:55.962
But you're gonna
have to dress appropriately

31:55.997 --> 31:57.496
around the house from now on.

31:58.603 --> 32:00.136
Yeah, of course. Sorry.

32:05.971 --> 32:07.539
Oh, Millie.

32:10.046 --> 32:12.214
Stay the fuck away
from my husband.

32:12.914 --> 32:14.447
(TENSE MUSIC PLAYS)

32:27.432 --> 32:29.163
(OVEN DINGS)

32:29.198 --> 32:31.029
-JILIANNE: Mmm.
-And so my nanny's going on

32:31.065 --> 32:33.231
and on about her dead dog,

32:33.267 --> 32:36.139
and I don't mean
to be a B-I-T-C-H,

32:36.175 --> 32:38.973
but since when did I become
a canine grief counselor?

32:39.009 --> 32:41.338
Meanwhile,
Emma is late for school.

32:41.373 --> 32:43.812
-WOMEN: Mmm.
-I'm missing yoga.

32:43.848 --> 32:45.113
You know what yoga means
to me.

32:45.148 --> 32:47.383
-It's everything.
-That's so unfortunate.

32:47.419 --> 32:48.516
Thank you.

32:48.552 --> 32:49.646
(INHALES)

32:49.682 --> 32:53.022
Well, we are going to be
looking for a nanny soon.

32:53.057 --> 32:55.088
(GASPS) Oh, my God, Nina!
You're pregnant.

32:55.123 --> 32:57.461
-Nina. (CHUCKLES)
-I knew it.

32:57.497 --> 32:59.563
No. Not... Not yet.

32:59.598 --> 33:01.392
We are making a plan.

33:01.427 --> 33:03.096
We've been going to see
this incredible

33:03.132 --> 33:04.733
fertility specialist
in the city.

33:04.768 --> 33:06.097
-Cool.
-Andrew insists

33:06.132 --> 33:07.702
on sparing no expense,

33:07.738 --> 33:09.302
of course. So, yeah.

33:09.337 --> 33:11.636
-That's wonderful.
-JILIANNE: Ooh, yeah.

33:11.672 --> 33:14.809
We will find you the most
fantastic nanny, I promise.

33:14.844 --> 33:16.175
-Absolutely.
-Thanks.

33:16.211 --> 33:18.475
Oh, this is
Cece's pediatrician.

33:18.510 --> 33:20.678
-I will be right back.
-SUZANNE: Oh.

33:21.685 --> 33:23.021
Fill our tea.

33:26.254 --> 33:27.351
JILIANNE: Oh, my God,
I'm so sorry.

33:27.387 --> 33:28.956
I really thought
she was pregnant.

33:28.992 --> 33:30.056
I know,
we were all thinking it.

33:30.092 --> 33:31.223
I mean,
have you seen her skin?

33:31.258 --> 33:32.796
God, and how about
those roots?

33:32.832 --> 33:33.963
My God.
You'd think she would take

33:33.998 --> 33:35.765
better care of herself
for Andrew.

33:35.801 --> 33:37.365
-He's so fucking hot.
-He is.

33:37.400 --> 33:39.967
And especially because
they have an airtight prenup.

33:40.003 --> 33:41.466
-JILIANNE: Mmm.
-Okay. You know,

33:41.502 --> 33:43.939
she did not have a dime
when they got married.

33:43.975 --> 33:45.271
She'll be sleeping
on the street

33:45.306 --> 33:46.636
if she doesn't get
her shit together.

33:46.671 --> 33:49.441
Cece? Would he get custody,
considering...

33:49.476 --> 33:52.545
PATRICE: Of course.
After what she did.

33:52.580 --> 33:54.844
How many months she spent
in that awful psych ward?

33:54.880 --> 33:56.884
-JILIANNE AND SUZANNE: Nine.
-(PATRICE CHUCKLING) Nine.

33:56.919 --> 33:58.115
Nine months. (SCOFFS)

33:58.150 --> 33:59.450
I mean, good Lord,

33:59.485 --> 34:00.889
I do not know
how he puts up with her.

34:00.925 --> 34:03.091
PATRICE:
Because he is a saint.

34:03.127 --> 34:04.522
-He's a hot saint.
-(PATRICE EXCLAIMS)

34:04.558 --> 34:08.062
-Hot Saint Andrew. Oh, my God.
-(ALL CHUCKLING)

34:08.098 --> 34:09.659
-SUZANNE: Ooh.
-What did I miss?

34:09.694 --> 34:12.735
Oh, we're just talking
spring fundraiser.

34:12.770 --> 34:13.802
-PATRICE: Ooh.
-Please,

34:13.838 --> 34:15.469
save us with a theme idea.

34:17.543 --> 34:19.571
Stop lurking.

34:19.606 --> 34:21.673
MILLIE: Those women were right
about one thing.

34:21.709 --> 34:24.543
 Andrew is definitely a saint
 for standing by Nina.

34:24.579 --> 34:26.983
 I can't believe she lied
 about being pregnant.

34:27.018 --> 34:29.184
 Everything she's told me
 is a lie.

34:29.220 --> 34:30.885
 It wasn't the hormones
 making her crazy.

34:30.920 --> 34:33.017
 She actually is crazy.

34:33.053 --> 34:34.254
 Poor Andrew.

34:34.290 --> 34:35.658
 As soon as I save up
 enough money,

34:35.694 --> 34:37.359
 I am out of here.

34:39.930 --> 34:42.100
Today wasn't a total disaster.

34:42.832 --> 34:44.596
Uh, thank you.

34:44.631 --> 34:46.631
I'm gonna need you
to watch Cece next Saturday.

34:46.666 --> 34:49.201
Andrew and I have
an appointment in the city,

34:49.236 --> 34:50.601
and I know it's your day off,

34:50.636 --> 34:53.311
but I trust
that it won't be a problem.

34:53.346 --> 34:54.409
Uh...

34:55.340 --> 34:57.544
-We'll have fun.
-Good.

35:25.940 --> 35:27.607
Haloperidol.

35:32.751 --> 35:34.845
Acute fucking psychosis?

35:38.419 --> 35:40.486
 Hey, Lexi,
 it's Millie. Listen.

35:40.521 --> 35:41.890
 I really need to make
 some extra money

35:41.925 --> 35:43.159
 so I can quit this job.

35:43.194 --> 35:45.391
Do you think
you could, um, ask your cousin

35:45.427 --> 35:47.996
if I could get a job
at the warehouse?

35:48.031 --> 35:49.164
I'll do anything. I'll clean,

35:49.199 --> 35:50.660
I'll set boxes,
I'll scrub toilets.

35:50.696 --> 35:52.965
I just really need
to get out of here.

35:53.001 --> 35:54.801
You're leaving?

35:54.836 --> 35:55.866
What?

35:56.267 --> 35:57.937
No, no, no.

35:57.972 --> 35:59.543
I'm gonna...

35:59.579 --> 36:00.739
make you lunch.

36:01.946 --> 36:03.207
What are you in the mood for?

36:03.243 --> 36:04.776
A bologna sandwich?

36:05.451 --> 36:06.512
Okay.

36:06.548 --> 36:09.016
But you said you needed
to get out of this place

36:09.051 --> 36:10.112
on the phone just now.

36:10.148 --> 36:11.621
No.

36:11.657 --> 36:12.850
You misheard me.

36:15.192 --> 36:17.426
One bologna sandwich
coming right up.

36:20.061 --> 36:22.128
So how was, uh...

36:22.164 --> 36:23.593
how was school this week?

36:23.629 --> 36:27.170
Learn anything fun
or interesting?

36:27.205 --> 36:30.307
It's school.
It's not fun or interesting.

36:31.006 --> 36:33.075
What about boys?

36:33.110 --> 36:34.737
-(EXCLAIMS)
-Got any crushes?

36:34.773 --> 36:37.108
Ew, no. Why would you even
ask me that?

36:37.143 --> 36:38.915
I am just...

36:38.951 --> 36:40.515
trying to make
some small talk.

36:41.554 --> 36:42.984
Forget it.

36:43.019 --> 36:44.321
I'm not hungry anyway.

36:47.053 --> 36:48.523
Okay.

36:52.494 --> 36:54.391
You don't have to be
my friend, you know.

36:54.427 --> 36:56.129
It's not part of your job.

36:56.164 --> 36:57.995
Well, I'd like to be.

36:58.031 --> 36:59.395
Why?

36:59.430 --> 37:01.165
'Cause I like you.

37:01.201 --> 37:02.537
No, you don't.

37:06.177 --> 37:07.611
CECE: "Do you want juice
 or water?"

37:07.647 --> 37:08.975
"Juice, please."

37:09.011 --> 37:10.209
"Don't spill.

37:10.244 --> 37:11.676
"Juice is a privilege."

37:11.711 --> 37:14.012
"I won't."
"Did you go to the salon today?"

37:14.047 --> 37:15.346
"Yes."

37:15.381 --> 37:16.549
"You look very nice."

37:16.584 --> 37:19.155
-"Thank you."
-Cece, would you like some

37:19.190 --> 37:20.786
dinosaur chicken nuggets
and ketchup?

37:21.420 --> 37:22.890
Ketchup makes a mess.

37:22.926 --> 37:24.287
Yes, it does.

37:24.322 --> 37:25.560
(CECE SIGHS)

37:26.028 --> 37:27.430
(MILLIE SIGHS)

37:31.268 --> 37:33.304
Cece, where did you find
this troll?

37:34.972 --> 37:36.701
Were you in my room?

37:36.736 --> 37:39.102
Cece, this troll is
very special to me.

37:39.137 --> 37:41.374
I don't want you going into
my room, do you understand?

37:41.410 --> 37:43.243
You need to stay
out of the attic.

37:43.278 --> 37:45.378
-So do you.
-(DOOR BANGING)

37:45.414 --> 37:47.417
-ANDREW: Hey.
-(NINA EXCLAIMING)

37:48.380 --> 37:50.521
(BREATH TREMBLING)

37:50.556 --> 37:51.586
(CRYING)

37:52.857 --> 37:55.354
(SIGHS) Hey, Cece,

37:55.390 --> 37:56.420
can you go play
in your bedroom

37:56.456 --> 37:57.724
for a little bit, please?

38:01.064 --> 38:03.034
(FOOTSTEPS RECEDING)

38:03.069 --> 38:04.267
-What happened?
-(TEAPOT WHISTLING)

38:04.302 --> 38:06.068
ANDREW: Premature
ovarian insufficiency.

38:06.103 --> 38:07.437
We've been trying for years.

38:07.939 --> 38:09.568
At least now we know.

38:09.603 --> 38:11.406
-I'm sorry.
-I've just... (SIGHS)

38:11.441 --> 38:14.211
Man, I've just always wanted
a lot of kids.

38:14.246 --> 38:16.743
Like a... Like a whole
soccer team full.

38:17.945 --> 38:20.081
(CLEARS THROAT) Nina and I
were only children like you.

38:20.116 --> 38:21.248
(CABINET KNOB CLICKS)

38:21.283 --> 38:22.512
Well, at least you have Cece.

38:22.547 --> 38:23.981
Of course, of course.

38:27.322 --> 38:28.920
I know it sounds selfish.

38:30.355 --> 38:32.021
I love Cece.

38:32.056 --> 38:34.424
I've always wanted a child
of my own with Nina.

38:34.460 --> 38:35.859
I didn't realize...

38:35.895 --> 38:39.997
Oh, Cece is...
she's absolutely my daughter.

38:40.832 --> 38:43.335
She's just not
my biological daughter.

38:43.370 --> 38:45.102
You're an amazing dad.

38:45.137 --> 38:47.910
Look, I just really don't know
how she's gonna take this.

38:47.945 --> 38:50.145
(BREATHES DEEPLY)

38:50.180 --> 38:51.745
She's been so fragile lately.

38:53.850 --> 38:57.787
I really don't think that she
can handle the disappointment.

38:57.822 --> 38:58.649
She has you.

38:58.685 --> 39:01.051
I don't think
that I am enough.

39:05.227 --> 39:06.496
(OBJECTS CLATTERING)

39:15.239 --> 39:16.505
-(NINA SCREAMING)
-(CLANKS)

39:16.540 --> 39:19.539
NINA: It's not fair!
I did everything I could!

39:19.574 --> 39:21.278
ANDREW: Nina,
it's not your fault.

39:21.313 --> 39:23.409
-(SHATTERING)
-NINA: You wish I was gone.

39:23.444 --> 39:24.674
ANDREW: God! Wait! Nina, no!

39:24.709 --> 39:25.841
-Hello?
-ANDREW: No, no, no!

39:25.877 --> 39:27.682
Andrew, are you...
are you okay?

39:29.182 --> 39:30.685
What?

39:33.484 --> 39:34.653
Oh, my God.

39:34.688 --> 39:37.821
-Andrew, are you okay?
-(CHUCKLING)

39:37.856 --> 39:40.557
What? You overheard
those PTA cunts

39:40.592 --> 39:42.165
saying that I'm crazy?

39:42.201 --> 39:44.463
That I don't deserve
my husband?

39:44.498 --> 39:46.767
That I belong in a nuthouse?

39:47.200 --> 39:48.571
Andrew!

39:54.440 --> 39:56.040
Let go of this.

39:57.844 --> 40:00.311
-Wrap this around your hand.
-Thank you.

40:00.347 --> 40:01.716
Alive and well.

40:14.162 --> 40:15.466
(SPRAYING)

40:18.870 --> 40:19.965
(SPRAYING)

40:27.538 --> 40:28.776
(NINA SIGHS)

40:29.744 --> 40:32.450
I cleaned up
the mess from last night.

40:34.319 --> 40:36.784
Sorry I wasn't honest
about the baby.

40:38.418 --> 40:40.055
I guess I was...

40:40.091 --> 40:41.756
trying to manifest.

40:43.027 --> 40:44.187
Or something.

40:46.660 --> 40:48.359
It's okay, I get it.
(CHUCKLES)

40:48.394 --> 40:52.228
I don't know... (CHUCKLING)
...how I'm gonna
face Andrew's mother.

40:56.467 --> 40:57.739
Anyway,

40:58.675 --> 41:01.011
I realized I need to stop
holding onto things

41:01.046 --> 41:02.873
and just start fresh.

41:02.908 --> 41:05.445
So these are
practically brand-new,

41:05.480 --> 41:07.584
and I want you to have them.

41:08.985 --> 41:10.015
I...

41:10.450 --> 41:11.954
I... I can't.

41:11.990 --> 41:13.083
No, seriously,

41:13.119 --> 41:15.422
these are gonna be thrown
in the bin at Goodwill.

41:15.458 --> 41:17.495
This would look
amazing on you.

41:18.095 --> 41:19.761
Millie, take it.

41:20.491 --> 41:21.694
Thanks.

41:21.729 --> 41:23.900
Well, Andrew took Cece
to pancakes,

41:23.935 --> 41:27.169
so you don't really have to
worry about breakfast
this morning.

41:27.204 --> 41:29.267
But I do need a favor.

41:29.302 --> 41:32.708
I need you to look into tickets
for a musical called Showdown.

41:33.508 --> 41:36.179
Andrew's been dying to see it,

41:36.214 --> 41:38.509
and I want to do something to

41:38.544 --> 41:40.518
make it up to him.

41:41.184 --> 41:42.413
Sure. (CHUCKLES)

41:42.449 --> 41:43.818
This Saturday,

41:44.352 --> 41:46.015
if you can manage,

41:46.050 --> 41:49.289
and an overnight
at a high-end hotel.

41:49.325 --> 41:50.422
Splurge on a suite.

41:50.458 --> 41:52.626
Something romantic.

41:52.661 --> 41:55.395
And Cece will be
at a friend's house.

41:55.431 --> 41:57.029
I'll arrange for her to...

41:58.334 --> 41:59.568
uh, be out of the house

41:59.604 --> 42:02.298
and you can just have
the weekend to yourself.

42:03.041 --> 42:05.042
That sounds great.

42:05.077 --> 42:06.836
I'll see what I can do.

42:06.871 --> 42:08.876
You're a lifesaver, Millie.

42:10.646 --> 42:12.847
I don't know
what I'd do without you.

42:13.249 --> 42:14.546
(CHUCKLES SOFTLY)

42:14.581 --> 42:18.589
(PIANO MUSIC PLAYING)

42:19.551 --> 42:20.921
(EXHALES)

42:24.561 --> 42:26.889
You're with
the Winchesters, right?

42:26.925 --> 42:29.600
-Yeah.
-I'm with the Leightons.

42:30.836 --> 42:32.000
Suzanne?

42:32.035 --> 42:33.098
Right.

42:34.305 --> 42:37.036
Cece's not that good, is she?

42:38.074 --> 42:39.607
(LAUGHS)

42:39.643 --> 42:42.171
Don't worry.
No one gives her any shit.

42:42.206 --> 42:44.340
Not after everything
she's been through.

42:45.743 --> 42:47.178
What do you mean?

42:47.546 --> 42:48.613
Seriously?

42:48.648 --> 42:50.752
All the psycho mom shit?

42:50.788 --> 42:53.316
I know she spent some time
in a psych ward, but...

42:56.092 --> 42:57.122
Um...

42:59.797 --> 43:03.997
Nina Winchester tried
to drown her kid in a bathtub.

43:04.729 --> 43:05.931
-What?
-Yeah.

43:05.966 --> 43:08.468
It's like all the PTA bitches
talk about.

43:08.503 --> 43:10.573
When Cece was a baby,

43:10.608 --> 43:13.539
Nina threw her
in a tub of running water,

43:13.575 --> 43:14.840
then tried to off herself

43:14.875 --> 43:17.106
by swallowing
a shit ton of pills.

43:17.141 --> 43:19.449
Luckily, her husband got
freaked out

43:19.484 --> 43:20.979
when he couldn't get
ahold of her,

43:21.015 --> 43:23.946
then called the police
for a wellness check.

43:23.981 --> 43:27.854
It's, like, fucked up, right?

43:27.889 --> 43:30.791
INSTRUCTOR: Great job,
dancers. Thank you.

43:30.827 --> 43:33.257
-Let's get our belongings.
-GIRL: All right.

43:37.595 --> 43:39.164
(SIGHS)

43:44.840 --> 43:47.370
-Your car smells like feet.
-Thank you.

43:52.181 --> 43:53.211
Hey.

43:55.014 --> 43:57.252
What do you know
about this family?

43:57.287 --> 43:58.417
Sorry, no English.

43:58.453 --> 43:59.822
Oh, bullshit.

44:01.821 --> 44:03.391
I know you shouldn't be here.

44:03.426 --> 44:06.059
-(DOOR OPENS)
-Why?

44:07.265 --> 44:08.361
NINA: Leave him alone.

44:08.397 --> 44:09.425
(DOOR CLOSES)

44:11.536 --> 44:13.836
You've no business
talking to Enzo.

44:14.602 --> 44:17.202
(SCOFFS) What is this?

44:17.238 --> 44:20.210
They're the Broadway tickets
and the hotel reservation.

44:20.245 --> 44:22.006
-For Saturday?
-Yeah.

44:22.041 --> 44:25.210
But why would I have you
book tickets...

44:25.246 --> 44:28.081
for the day that I'm driving
Cece to arts camp in D.C.?

44:28.116 --> 44:30.647
-Why would I do that?
-I don't know, but you did.

44:30.683 --> 44:32.483
No, I didn't.

44:32.518 --> 44:36.152
And I assume that these
are non-refundable now,
at this point?

44:36.187 --> 44:38.387
Nina, I did
what you asked me to do.

44:38.422 --> 44:40.390
Fine. They're gonna
come out of your paycheck.

44:40.425 --> 44:42.565
And I'm so sorry about that,
but it was your mistake,

44:42.600 --> 44:44.498
and you're gonna have to cover
the fee.

44:44.534 --> 44:46.168
Nina, I can't afford that.

44:46.204 --> 44:47.197
I don't care!

44:47.232 --> 44:48.802
It was your mistake.
You're gonna cover it.

44:48.837 --> 44:50.874
Nina, that's more
than I have saved.

44:50.910 --> 44:52.538
Hey.

44:52.574 --> 44:54.008
-Hello.
-NINA: Hi.

44:57.549 --> 44:58.947
Just about
cleaned out the florist,

44:58.983 --> 45:01.719
so otherwise I would have...
I would have got you more.

45:02.385 --> 45:03.721
What's wrong?

45:04.421 --> 45:05.753
Millie booked tickets

45:05.788 --> 45:07.917
for a non-refundable weekend
for us

45:07.952 --> 45:10.759
that we can't even use.

45:10.794 --> 45:12.956
And she's gonna have
to pay for it. Sorry.

45:12.991 --> 45:14.491
No, she doesn't.
That's okay.

45:14.527 --> 45:16.432
We'll just call the credit card
company and have it reversed.

45:16.467 --> 45:17.699
I don't think that's a thing.

45:17.734 --> 45:19.932
ANDREW: That is a thing.
That's a thing.

45:19.967 --> 45:22.135
You don't have to pay
for anything.

45:22.503 --> 45:23.774
Thank you.

45:24.307 --> 45:25.809
I'm sorry.

45:30.180 --> 45:31.276
(SIGHS)

45:34.350 --> 45:35.478
Sweetheart?

45:43.359 --> 45:45.023
(SOFT THUDS)

45:45.058 --> 45:46.495
ANDREW: All this stuff
for a week?

45:46.531 --> 45:48.898
I don't want her
to get homesick.

45:51.830 --> 45:53.331
(ENGINE STARTS)

45:55.801 --> 45:59.073
(WATER RUNNING)

46:15.723 --> 46:18.191
Okay. Sorry. Shit. Okay.

46:18.558 --> 46:19.830
Sorry.

46:27.335 --> 46:30.466
I am so sorry. I usually get
dressed before I come out.

46:30.502 --> 46:33.303
No, it's really my fault.
I was actually just...

46:33.338 --> 46:35.945
I was coming
to confess something to you.

46:37.644 --> 46:41.247
I wanted to let you know
that I couldn't get
the tickets refunded.

46:41.979 --> 46:43.887
-Shit.
-Yeah.

46:46.954 --> 46:49.625
So I think
you should take them

46:49.661 --> 46:51.388
and go to the show
with a friend

46:51.424 --> 46:53.829
and stay in the room,
charge whatever you want.

46:53.865 --> 46:56.460
Room service.
I want you to enjoy yourself.

46:57.367 --> 46:58.896
That is...

46:58.932 --> 47:01.804
really nice of you, but...

47:01.839 --> 47:04.341
I can't. I don't have anyone
I can bring.

47:04.376 --> 47:06.272
You gotta have somebody.

47:08.139 --> 47:10.045
I wish I did, but I don't.

47:11.217 --> 47:12.542
(ANDREW SIGHS)

47:16.052 --> 47:19.120
Okay, well, just, um...
how about you and I go?

47:20.186 --> 47:22.959
We can come back tonight.
I can...

47:23.893 --> 47:25.191
I can sweeten the deal
a little bit,

47:25.227 --> 47:28.261
throw in a slice of pizza,
maybe a hot apple cider?

47:28.929 --> 47:31.099
I'll just tell Nina that I...

47:31.134 --> 47:33.470
exchanged the tickets
and I can take her next week.

47:33.505 --> 47:35.431
No, I can't have you do that.

47:35.466 --> 47:37.704
Oh, come on, we could both
use a night out.

47:37.739 --> 47:40.370
I know we could.
Why not?

47:40.405 --> 47:42.946
I mean, it's supposed to be
a great show.

47:44.578 --> 47:45.641
Okay.

47:46.880 --> 47:49.084
Great. We're going.

47:51.690 --> 47:53.983
(CINNAMON GIRL BY LANA DEL REY
PLAYING)

47:54.019 --> 47:55.585
♪ Cinnamon ♪

47:57.792 --> 47:59.963
♪ In my teeth ♪

48:01.159 --> 48:03.494
♪ From your kiss ♪

48:04.569 --> 48:07.369
♪ You're touching me ♪

48:07.404 --> 48:08.669
Great dress.

48:08.705 --> 48:10.908
♪ All the pills ♪

48:11.675 --> 48:14.108
♪ That you take ♪

48:14.144 --> 48:17.648
♪ Violet, blue, green
 red to keep me ♪

48:17.683 --> 48:21.145
♪ At arm's length don't work ♪

48:21.180 --> 48:23.719
♪ You try to push me out ♪

48:23.754 --> 48:25.553
♪ But I just find my... ♪

48:25.588 --> 48:27.849
Thanks for coming.

48:27.885 --> 48:33.193
♪ Violet, blue, green, red
 to keep me out, I win ♪

48:33.228 --> 48:36.733
♪ There's things
 I wanna say to you ♪

48:36.768 --> 48:39.563
♪ But I'll just let you live ♪

48:39.598 --> 48:43.302
♪ Like if you hold me
 without hurting me ♪

48:43.337 --> 48:46.877
♪ You'll be the first
 who ever did ♪

48:46.912 --> 48:50.372
♪ There's things
 I wanna talk about ♪

48:50.407 --> 48:53.544
♪ But better not to give ♪

48:53.579 --> 48:57.448
♪ But if you hold me
 without hurting me ♪

48:57.483 --> 49:01.354
♪ You'll be the first
 who ever did ♪

49:08.492 --> 49:11.430
♪ Be the first who ever did ♪

49:12.770 --> 49:14.166
-I'm hungry.
-Yeah, I'm hungry.

49:14.202 --> 49:16.398
-I could eat. Yeah.
-Yeah? (CHUCKLES)

49:16.434 --> 49:18.101
Wasn't pizza
a part of this deal?

49:18.136 --> 49:19.668
-Yeah, it was.
-Yeah?

49:19.704 --> 49:23.208
Yeah. You know what?
I think I got a better idea.

49:23.243 --> 49:24.842
MILLIE: Holy shit,
that was amazing.

49:24.878 --> 49:26.011
(ANDREW SIGHS)

49:26.046 --> 49:27.515
-It was, wasn't it?
-Yeah.

49:27.551 --> 49:28.612
ANDREW: Yeah.

49:29.887 --> 49:32.114
MILLIE: This place is
really fancy.

49:32.150 --> 49:33.855
Well, it's charming,

49:33.890 --> 49:35.522
in an old New York
kind of way.

49:35.557 --> 49:36.920
Yeah.

49:36.956 --> 49:38.325
I... I don't...

49:38.360 --> 49:40.029
(CHUCKLING) I don't really
know what I should order.

49:40.064 --> 49:41.928
Well, how about we just get
one of everything?

49:41.963 --> 49:43.196
-Everything?
-Everything.

49:43.232 --> 49:46.102
-(CHUCKLING) We can't do that.
-Yeah, we can.

49:49.067 --> 49:50.436
You like martinis?

49:51.004 --> 49:52.171
I guess. I don't know.

49:52.206 --> 49:54.070
-Well, I guess we'll find out.
-Yeah.

49:54.105 --> 49:55.476
To new adventures.

49:55.511 --> 49:56.607
Cheers.

50:01.512 --> 50:02.852
ANDREW: I mean,
you're funny, you're...

50:02.887 --> 50:04.352
you're caring,
you're great with kids.

50:04.387 --> 50:06.417
I just don't understand why
you're cleaning people's houses.

50:06.453 --> 50:08.990
You should be out there
living your best life.

50:09.025 --> 50:10.586
And have you ever thought
about what

50:10.622 --> 50:13.624
you want to do with your time
on this Earth?

50:14.493 --> 50:17.760
-I don't know. No, not really.
-Why not?

50:18.602 --> 50:19.930
(MILLIE INHALES)

50:19.966 --> 50:21.062
What about you?

50:21.098 --> 50:22.397
Are you...

50:22.432 --> 50:25.169
living your best life doing...

50:25.204 --> 50:27.072
I don't even know what you do.

50:27.107 --> 50:28.776
I run a data processing company

50:28.811 --> 50:30.847
that my father left me.

50:30.882 --> 50:32.879
Basically, I get paid
a lot of money

50:32.915 --> 50:35.283
to do really boring shit.

50:35.318 --> 50:38.053
-Gotcha.
-I mean, all I've ever
really wanted to do

50:38.088 --> 50:40.684
was to be a husband
and a father, honestly.

50:41.219 --> 50:43.023
That's really sweet.

50:43.059 --> 50:45.359
What about you?
Do you want kids?

50:46.430 --> 50:47.493
Yeah.

50:47.992 --> 50:49.231
Someday.

50:50.231 --> 50:52.168
With the right person,
of course.

50:52.702 --> 50:53.929
I mean, I... I...

50:53.964 --> 50:56.203
feel like I won the lottery
with Nina, and I should feel

50:56.239 --> 50:58.705
-like I'm living my best life.
-But you're not?

50:58.741 --> 51:00.410
I love my wife.

51:00.445 --> 51:02.143
I really do.

51:02.178 --> 51:04.207
I just feel like
she's angry all the time,

51:04.242 --> 51:05.677
and I don't know why.

51:05.712 --> 51:08.514
I feel like every conversation
we have ends in a tirade.

51:09.517 --> 51:12.386
If it makes you feel
any better, same. (CHUCKLES)

51:12.421 --> 51:15.624
I mean, she used to be
so different. She was, uh...

51:15.659 --> 51:17.422
She was... loving,

51:17.457 --> 51:19.723
and she was kind,
and she was generous.

51:20.324 --> 51:22.064
She was affectionate.

51:22.099 --> 51:24.767
I mean, all I want to do is
make her happy

51:24.803 --> 51:26.702
and I genuinely
don't know how.

51:26.737 --> 51:28.402
Andrew, it's not you.

51:29.601 --> 51:31.538
I should not have said that.
I'm sorry.

51:31.573 --> 51:33.168
No, it's okay. I mean, I see
the way that she treats you,

51:33.204 --> 51:34.870
and I hate it.

51:36.778 --> 51:37.840
I hate it.

51:39.445 --> 51:41.712
I feel like
I'm letting you down.

51:42.454 --> 51:43.483
You're not.

51:49.060 --> 51:51.293
Pretty sure there's
a dance floor in there.

51:53.729 --> 51:54.723
(CHUCKLES)

51:54.758 --> 51:57.093
-You want to go dancing?
-Should we hit it?

51:57.128 --> 51:58.698
(CHUCKLING)

51:58.733 --> 51:59.796
Yeah.

52:01.099 --> 52:02.335
Let's dance.

52:02.370 --> 52:07.342
♪ Will your eyes
 return to mine? ♪

52:09.146 --> 52:13.183
♪ Will our day start
 to shine? ♪

52:13.851 --> 52:15.679
♪ It was winter ♪

52:15.714 --> 52:22.759
♪ Now let's move
 right into spring ♪

52:22.794 --> 52:26.394
♪ Let the birds sing ♪

52:29.634 --> 52:31.568
(FAINT CLAPPING)

52:31.603 --> 52:33.170
(ANDREW CHUCKLES)

52:34.536 --> 52:37.867
I don't suppose you feel sober
enough to drive us home?

52:38.973 --> 52:40.474
Not really, no.

52:41.472 --> 52:42.905
I think we got a problem.

52:46.611 --> 52:50.385
RECEPTIONIST:
And you're all set.

52:50.420 --> 52:52.348
They're not adjoining,
but they're on the same floor.

52:52.383 --> 52:54.757
-Thanks.
-ANDREW: Mm.

52:54.792 --> 52:55.886
Shit, my phone's dead.

52:55.922 --> 52:57.227
Oh.

52:58.192 --> 52:59.491
-Here you go.
-Thank you.

52:59.526 --> 53:02.225
-Of course. Have a great stay.
-Thank you.

53:02.260 --> 53:04.333
(THUNDER RUMBLING)

53:06.803 --> 53:08.370
(ELEVATOR DINGS)

53:30.125 --> 53:31.789
I'll see you in the morning.

53:33.862 --> 53:35.265
Good night.

53:51.681 --> 53:52.777
(SIGHS)

53:53.551 --> 53:54.581
(SIGHS)

53:58.886 --> 53:59.916
(SIGHS)

54:01.693 --> 54:03.260
(WATER RUNNING)

54:09.131 --> 54:11.626
Do not blow up your life.

54:11.661 --> 54:14.066
-(THUNDER RUMBLING)
-(SIGHS)

54:14.101 --> 54:15.866
(PHONE VIBRATING)

54:22.845 --> 54:24.042
Oh, shit.

54:24.078 --> 54:26.316
(THUNDERCLAP)

54:27.079 --> 54:28.384
(GASPS)

54:28.817 --> 54:30.150
Oh, no.

54:30.185 --> 54:32.817
-(KNOCKING AT DOOR)
-Hey.

54:33.725 --> 54:34.951
What's wrong?

54:39.494 --> 54:41.363
She doesn't mean it.
I'll talk to her.

54:41.399 --> 54:43.662
-She does, Andrew. She does.
-Millie, come here.

54:43.697 --> 54:45.329
(VOICE SHAKING) She wants
to destroy my life,

54:45.364 --> 54:46.630
and I don't know why.

54:46.665 --> 54:49.370
No, she doesn't.
I will talk to her.

54:49.406 --> 54:51.840
Andrew, I know you think
that I can do better,

54:51.876 --> 54:53.640
but I need this job.

54:53.675 --> 54:56.475
I can't lose it. I... I...
I do not want to go back.

54:56.510 --> 55:00.280
-Go back where?
-(THUNDER RUMBLING)

55:00.316 --> 55:01.710
You're not going
to lose your job.

55:01.746 --> 55:03.782
Everything is going
to be okay.

55:04.648 --> 55:06.589
-I promise you.
-(SNIFFLES)

55:06.624 --> 55:07.819
Okay?

55:09.190 --> 55:11.761
Don't cry. It's okay.

55:11.797 --> 55:12.926
It's gonna be okay.

55:12.962 --> 55:14.364
(MILLIE SIGHS)

55:15.030 --> 55:16.430
(THUNDER RUMBLING)

55:16.465 --> 55:17.729
(BAD AS THE REST BY
JESSIE MURPH PLAYING)

55:17.764 --> 55:20.269
♪ Fool me once
 and it's "So what?" ♪

55:20.304 --> 55:22.737
♪ Fool me twice
 I'm a dumb fuck ♪

55:22.772 --> 55:26.270
♪ Three times, you like
 every damn boy I ever loved ♪

55:26.305 --> 55:27.637
♪ Oh, no ♪

55:27.673 --> 55:29.809
(MILLIE MOANS)
Take off my dress.

55:29.844 --> 55:32.415
♪ You're telling me
 that you're the exception ♪

55:32.450 --> 55:34.476
♪ If you a good boy
 with bad intentions ♪

55:34.511 --> 55:35.819
(ZIPPER UNZIPPING)

55:35.854 --> 55:38.318
♪ Tell me now ♪

55:38.353 --> 55:40.517
♪ 'Cause it's kinda late ♪

55:40.552 --> 55:43.192
♪ And I'm emotionally ♪

55:43.227 --> 55:47.022
♪ Kinda twisted right around ♪

55:47.057 --> 55:49.496
♪ And if I stay
 another minute, babe ♪

55:49.531 --> 55:52.061
♪ I'll say a thing
 I never say ♪

55:52.097 --> 55:55.797
♪ 'Cause something
 'bout you breaks me down ♪

55:55.832 --> 56:00.674
♪ I do not love you yet ♪

56:00.709 --> 56:05.576
♪ But I'm 'bout
 as close as I can get ♪

56:05.611 --> 56:08.248
♪ Keep one last percent ♪

56:08.283 --> 56:10.585
♪ Close to my chest ♪

56:10.620 --> 56:15.651
♪ Just in case
you turn out bad as the rest ♪

56:15.686 --> 56:20.255
♪ I will not be a fool ♪

56:20.290 --> 56:25.497
♪ But for you, I might do
 what dumb bitches do ♪

56:25.533 --> 56:27.935
♪ Put on the dress say... ♪

56:27.971 --> 56:29.769
(MOANS SOFTLY)

56:30.369 --> 56:31.902
(THUNDERCLAP)

56:31.938 --> 56:34.671
♪ ...heart
 from my place to your bed ♪

56:34.706 --> 56:38.448
♪ I'm as bad as the rest ♪

56:38.916 --> 56:40.813
(THUNDERCLAP)

56:45.123 --> 56:50.922
♪ I'm as bad as the rest ♪

56:59.099 --> 57:00.767
(SIGHS)

57:02.634 --> 57:04.166
Nina's coming home early.

57:05.538 --> 57:07.202
So we have to beat her home.

57:09.211 --> 57:10.546
We should get going.

57:11.113 --> 57:12.614
-Okay.
-Okay?

57:14.450 --> 57:16.048
This is gonna sound
really cheesy,

57:16.084 --> 57:19.753
but I didn't think anybody
could look so beautiful
in the morning.

57:29.726 --> 57:31.501
Nina can't ever know.

57:32.666 --> 57:35.337
And this can't
ever happen again.

57:35.372 --> 57:37.573
I really wish
things were different.

57:38.804 --> 57:41.236
I wish I would have
met you before.

57:42.714 --> 57:43.744
Me too.

57:44.278 --> 57:45.515
Are you okay?

57:45.981 --> 57:47.110
Yeah.

57:52.218 --> 57:53.655
(SIGHS)

58:16.374 --> 58:17.877
Nina?

58:23.084 --> 58:24.213
Nina!

58:26.091 --> 58:29.086
I'm gonna go get changed.

58:29.121 --> 58:32.089
I'll start making lunch
just in case she comes back.

58:49.947 --> 58:51.779
Ah, fuck it.

59:17.204 --> 59:18.234
Hello?

59:21.045 --> 59:22.106
Anybody home?

59:25.180 --> 59:26.308
(OVEN DINGS)

59:27.346 --> 59:28.717
Hi.

59:29.383 --> 59:31.420
Welcome home.

59:31.455 --> 59:34.250
-Thank you.
-Lunch is almost ready.

59:34.892 --> 59:36.758
Oh, boy.

59:37.294 --> 59:39.761
-Hi.
-Hey, sweetheart.

59:39.796 --> 59:42.797
-Hi. What are you doing?
-I was just fixing the drain

59:42.832 --> 59:45.399
in the upstairs guest bathroom.
It's a bit clogged.

59:45.435 --> 59:46.865
I knew you would
try to do that.

59:46.900 --> 59:48.329
I said the plumber's coming
on Tuesday.

59:48.365 --> 59:50.270
No, I know. I was just
feeling extra manly today.

59:50.305 --> 59:52.406
-Okay.
-Yeah.

59:52.441 --> 59:54.042
How was the trip? How's Cece?

59:54.077 --> 59:55.678
She's good.

59:57.013 --> 59:58.710
Listen.

59:58.746 --> 01:00:00.650
I'm very sorry
about last night.

01:00:01.648 --> 01:00:03.318
It was a very long drive.

01:00:03.353 --> 01:00:04.748
I was very tired. (CHUCKLES)

01:00:04.783 --> 01:00:07.021
I do not sleep well in hotels,

01:00:07.057 --> 01:00:08.084
turns out.

01:00:08.120 --> 01:00:10.723
And I should not be left alone
with my phone.

01:00:10.758 --> 01:00:14.322
So, lesson learned.
It's a new day.

01:00:14.357 --> 01:00:16.960
-Please accept my apologies.
-Yeah, it's okay.

01:00:16.996 --> 01:00:18.962
-I'm sorry. I'm so sorry.
-It's okay.

01:00:18.998 --> 01:00:21.136
-(EXHALES)
-Let's get some food in ya.

01:00:21.171 --> 01:00:22.064
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

01:00:22.099 --> 01:00:24.707
-NINA: Mm. Mm.
-NINA AND ANDREW: Hi.

01:00:25.508 --> 01:00:27.644
-This looks fantastic.
-Yes.

01:00:29.377 --> 01:00:31.444
(BREATHES DEEPLY)

01:00:31.480 --> 01:00:33.449
...you know? Hey, Millie.

01:00:33.484 --> 01:00:36.147
-MILLIE: Mm-hmm.
-How was your night off?

01:00:37.553 --> 01:00:40.014
Uh, my best friend Lexi
took me

01:00:40.050 --> 01:00:42.417
-to Peter Luger.
-ANDREW: Hmm.

01:00:42.452 --> 01:00:44.622
Um, she had a gift certificate.
It was really nice.

01:00:44.657 --> 01:00:46.423
We had a lot of sides.

01:00:46.459 --> 01:00:47.659
(CHUCKLES)

01:00:47.694 --> 01:00:49.630
But I don't really eat meat.

01:00:49.665 --> 01:00:51.930
This looks incredible.
So, thank you.

01:00:51.966 --> 01:00:55.601
I don't know why
but my quiches never turn out.

01:00:55.636 --> 01:00:57.003
I've been meaning to ask you.

01:00:57.038 --> 01:00:59.307
Did you learn how to cook
while you were in prison?

01:00:59.342 --> 01:01:00.402
(TENSE MUSIC PLAYING)

01:01:02.173 --> 01:01:03.973
You know, she was in prison
for ten years

01:01:04.009 --> 01:01:06.012
before she came to
work with us.

01:01:07.083 --> 01:01:08.344
Right?

01:01:09.418 --> 01:01:10.753
I think it's brave,

01:01:11.621 --> 01:01:15.119
making a new start
in a new town.

01:01:15.155 --> 01:01:18.321
I'm glad that we could be
a part of your journey.

01:01:20.295 --> 01:01:21.423
(NINA SIPS)

01:01:24.298 --> 01:01:26.228
Oh.

01:01:26.264 --> 01:01:28.831
We need a restock
of all of Cece's favorites

01:01:28.866 --> 01:01:30.100
before she gets home.

01:01:30.136 --> 01:01:32.401
You haven't really been
keeping up with that.

01:01:33.244 --> 01:01:35.837
And could you... Sorry.

01:01:35.873 --> 01:01:36.907
Could you use my car

01:01:36.943 --> 01:01:38.174
for running errands
from now on

01:01:38.210 --> 01:01:39.678
until you can save up
to get something nicer?

01:01:39.713 --> 01:01:41.717
I'm afraid yours is becoming

01:01:41.753 --> 01:01:44.446
an unwelcome topic
of conversation. Here you go.

01:01:45.621 --> 01:01:47.218
-You know what I mean?
-Yeah.

01:01:47.818 --> 01:01:50.023
(SIGHS) You okay?

01:01:51.523 --> 01:01:52.993
Yeah.

01:01:56.598 --> 01:01:58.193
MILLIE: I had it all wrong.

01:01:58.228 --> 01:01:59.895
 Nina was never
 one of those women

01:01:59.931 --> 01:02:01.367
 just going with her gut.

01:02:01.402 --> 01:02:02.502
 She knew.

01:02:02.537 --> 01:02:03.872
 The whole fucking time,

01:02:03.907 --> 01:02:06.070
 she knew I needed this job
 and couldn't leave,

01:02:06.105 --> 01:02:08.909
 no matter how shitty
 she made my life.

01:02:08.945 --> 01:02:11.308
 What kind of bitch
 does something like that?

01:02:12.912 --> 01:02:15.015
CASHIER: Thanks,
have a good day.

01:02:17.386 --> 01:02:19.114
Hello, Millie.

01:02:19.149 --> 01:02:21.855
-Hi.
-Is that the newest phone?

01:02:21.890 --> 01:02:24.424
What do you think
of that camera? It's...

01:02:24.460 --> 01:02:26.155
pretty great, right?

01:02:26.190 --> 01:02:28.224
I wouldn't know.
I only use it for work.

01:02:28.259 --> 01:02:31.064
Well, still, you're very
trusting. (CHUCKLES)

01:02:31.598 --> 01:02:32.900
What do you mean?

01:02:32.936 --> 01:02:35.604
Pumpkin, most of the nannies
won't take the phone

01:02:35.639 --> 01:02:37.332
'cause they don't want
every text,

01:02:37.367 --> 01:02:40.005
every call,
every place you go tracked.

01:02:40.040 --> 01:02:42.705
But, I mean,
you have nothing to hide, so...

01:02:42.741 --> 01:02:44.011
good for you.

01:02:45.144 --> 01:02:47.383
MILLIE: And that's
 when I realized

01:02:47.418 --> 01:02:49.148
 that Nina knew everything.

01:02:51.014 --> 01:02:52.349
(TENSE MUSIC PLAYING)

01:02:56.253 --> 01:02:58.724
-OFFICER: Millie Calloway.
-Yeah?

01:02:58.759 --> 01:03:00.491
Hands against the car, please.

01:03:00.527 --> 01:03:01.826
What? Why?

01:03:01.862 --> 01:03:03.496
I said,
"Hands against the car."

01:03:03.531 --> 01:03:04.895
Ow! What did I do?

01:03:04.931 --> 01:03:07.228
This car's been
reported stolen.

01:03:07.264 --> 01:03:08.535
-What? No.
-(HANDCUFFS RATCHETING)

01:03:08.571 --> 01:03:10.268
No, this is my boss's car.

01:03:11.142 --> 01:03:12.237
(RATCHETING)

01:03:18.447 --> 01:03:20.875
(BREATH TREMBLING)

01:03:20.911 --> 01:03:22.379
(SIREN CHIRPS)

01:03:40.965 --> 01:03:43.169
(SPEAKING INDISTINCTLY)

01:03:43.802 --> 01:03:45.066
ANDREW: Thank you.

01:03:45.102 --> 01:03:47.910
(INDISTINCT CONVERSATION)

01:03:56.154 --> 01:03:57.315
I'm sorry.

